Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||10-28-2001||05:48 AM||||Yes, firewalls are usually cause for errors. If you get an error at startup, it's usually a corrupted config file. Try uninstalling PIP first, then completely wipe the folder where you installed PIP in (usually /Program Files/pip/) then reinstall. See if that works.||||reg||1
